WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.670
- So, there is this app that's
a trivia game called HQ.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.830
I'm sure you guys have played it.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.030
Everyone's talking about it.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.230
I actually haven't played it yet.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.530
But someone just told me that
you can win money playing HQ.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.810
I like money, so I thought, you know what?

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.680
I'm gonna download, but
I'm not just gonna try it.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.290
I'm gonna win it, but I'm
not just gonna win it.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.140
I'm gonna master it, but
I'm not just gonna master--

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.670
Yeah, the joke was over
about a minute ago.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.699
Let's go play some HQ.

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:19.736
(intense music)

00:00:19.736 --> 00:00:21.510
All right, so I just downloaded HQ.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.680
I'm actually pretty nervous.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.660
I really hope that this video

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.060
is just like one minute long.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.830
It's my into and then just
me mastering it immediately.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:28.663
This is weird.

00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:30.650
The app is very like old school.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.270
And there's just comments nonstop.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.780
Scott, Scotty, Scott.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.500
So, I have three minutes
'til the game starts.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.660
And I guess I'll just take this time

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.610
to kind of prepare, a little training.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.740
Two plus two equals four.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.970
Finish this sentence,
Mickey Mouse Clubhouse.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.660
List the presidents in order.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.100
George Washington.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.683
(gentle music)

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.720
All right, the game started.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.380
720,000 people playing.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.240
I can beat 720,000 people easy.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.890
- [Host] $2,000!

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.820
Question one, which of these creatures

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.270
is most likely to bark?

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.270
Mime, did you bark up the
right tree, and pick dog?

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:11.644
Which of these things is
not found inside an atom?

00:01:11.644 --> 00:01:13.940
Proton, wonton?

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.460
The answer is wonton.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.940
Which of these is not the
title of a current TV show?

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:24.801
Chicago Med, Chicago
Fire, or Chicago Police?

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:27.100
Chicago Police.
- No!

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.550
Chicago PD, that's a show.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.992
PD means police, right?

00:01:31.992 --> 00:01:34.850
(gentle music)

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.920
I'm so upset, I could have easily won.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.753
Let me see.

00:01:37.753 --> 00:01:40.350
- [Host] Who was not a wife of Henry VIII?

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.593
Catherine Parr?
- Catherine Howard.

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:45.050
How I am supposed to know this stuff?

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.840
Catherine Howard sounds
like a friend of my mom's.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.100
- [Eric Voiceover] Even
though I was frustrated,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.690
I kept playing.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.660
I had hope that I could win this game,

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.900
and I played every chance I got.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.506
Only problem was that I kept losing.

00:01:58.506 --> 00:01:59.490
(gentle music)

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.688
Over, and over again.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.320
(gentle music)

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.520
But then, I got an idea.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.770
- I'm just gonna go around the office,

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.510
see who knows HQ best,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.860
and see if they wanna join my HQ team.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.870
Do you know HQ?
- Headquarters?

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.880
- No, not headquarters, the game HQ.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.880
- No, I'm actually not familiar with it.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.280
- Do you know what HQ is?

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.482
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah?

00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:24.280
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
(laughs)

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.610
- I'm trying to make a team.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.600
So, that we can win every single time.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.433
- Sure, sure, sure, sure, sure.

00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:29.910
That's a fantastic idea.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.010
- So, do you guys like split

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.820
the five dollar earnings if you win?

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.650
- [Cameraman] How well
thought out is this team?

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:37.483
- Not at all.

00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:38.880
Which of these cities was never

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.714
a capital of the Persian empire?

00:02:40.714 --> 00:02:42.697
Oh, I can't pronounce any of these.

00:02:42.697 --> 00:02:43.530
(all laugh)

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.286
Nineveh, Baghdad, Pasar-ga-driah.

00:02:46.286 --> 00:02:48.810
Okay, skip this question,
'cause I can't pronounce it.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.240
Which TV show was rebooted as a sequel,

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.606
but with new actors as
the same characters?

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.660
MacGyver (laughing).

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.320
Which of these snacks was founded

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.340
in Finland dating back
to around 6,000 B.C?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.250
Potato chips, chewing gum, cheese sticks.

00:03:05.307 --> 00:03:07.377
- (grunting) Cheese sticks.

00:03:07.377 --> 00:03:08.620
- Dave my man.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.453
- Did I get it?

00:03:09.453 --> 00:03:10.286
- No.

00:03:10.286 --> 00:03:13.900
- Wait a second, you're
not Scott, get outta here.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.010
- Actress Emma Watson
studied at which University?

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.410
Harvard, Brown, or Cambridge?

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.243
- Brown.

00:03:18.243 --> 00:03:19.076
- You are correct.

00:03:19.076 --> 00:03:19.909
Sarah, you know what?

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:20.742
Four for four, that's good enough,

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:21.575
I think you've made the team.

00:03:21.575 --> 00:03:22.810
- Those were just, oh,
I want more questions.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:23.680
- [Cameraman] We have more questions,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.250
I feel like you're not
doing this very well.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.260
- No, but I just, I'm sick
of trying to find this team,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.880
so I'm just gonna accept four.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.810
- [Cameraman] So it's just
gonna be you and Sarah?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.340
- No, no, no, I mean so far yes.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.370
- [Cameraman] That's not a team.

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:37.350
- [Eric Voiceover] My cameraman was right.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.750
I had to step up my game, I had to talk to

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.699
everyone in the office and
form the ultimate HQ team.

00:03:41.699 --> 00:03:43.060
(intense music)

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:43.958
That's what I did.

00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:45.830
We were confident.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.130
Yeah we were, we were a little too conf--

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.227
We were really confident.

00:03:50.227 --> 00:03:53.310
(upbeat funky music)

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.438
- [Host] How many US state names
are only four letters long?

00:03:55.438 --> 00:03:57.110
- That's such a hard question,

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.619
if we all get out on two right now.

00:03:58.619 --> 00:03:59.849
(all laughing)

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:01.220
- [Group] Iowa, Iowa...

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.128
- Clearly it's three,
we can't be that bad.

00:04:03.128 --> 00:04:04.067
(all laughing)

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.220
(all cheering)

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.089
- [Guy] It's between two and three.

00:04:06.089 --> 00:04:08.048
- Yes, yes, no, it's the oboe.

00:04:08.048 --> 00:04:09.530
- Woo

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.350
- Not gonna toot my oboe.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.780
- Oh, snap, snap, snap.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.880
- [Eric Voiceover] We were doing so well,

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.730
I thought we were all gonna
win, until this one question.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.870
- [Guy] What, what's a glabella?

00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:23.872
- [Girl] I'm gonna say Phelps,
I don't know what that means.

00:04:23.872 --> 00:04:25.053
- [Guy] Dammit.

00:04:25.053 --> 00:04:26.315
(all yelling)

00:04:26.315 --> 00:04:27.980
- [Eric] Everyone's out.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.813
- Oh, I'm in!

00:04:28.813 --> 00:04:29.861
(all cheering)

00:04:29.861 --> 00:04:32.572
- [Eric Voiceover] We made
it to the final round.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.805
(all cheering)

00:04:33.805 --> 00:04:36.472
(intense music)

00:04:38.784 --> 00:04:39.864
- [Guy] Bradley Cooper, Bradley Cooper.

00:04:39.864 --> 00:04:41.413
- That's such an easy question.

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:42.852
- [Eric Voiceover] It
was an easy question.

00:04:42.852 --> 00:04:44.875
And so we won.

00:04:44.875 --> 00:04:46.440
(all cheering)

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.250
But I wasn't satisfied, because
I wasn't the one who won,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.050
and that's what I set
out to do in this video.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.300
So there was more work to be done.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.133
- So I'm gonna talk to some
of the best HQ players,

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.880
and see what advice they have.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.880
- Hi, I'm Jamie Ortiz.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.773
I'm the HQ trivia winner for $6,000.00.

00:05:00.773 --> 00:05:01.890
- What?

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:04.850
Wait, I didn't know that,
are you the top winner?

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.150
- There's another guy named Casey Donahue.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.205
- I'm Casey Donahue, I'm one of the

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:12.040
all time winners on HQ trivia.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.560
- Hey I'm Zach Kornfeld,
I work at Buzzfeed.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.910
I'm one of the Try Guys,
and I'm also an Hqtie.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.160
What you might not know about me,

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.395
is that I'm a four time HQ champion.

00:05:19.395 --> 00:05:21.435
- I've been playing HQ
for like two weeks now

00:05:21.435 --> 00:05:25.230
and I have had no luck,
do you have any advice?

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.410
How do I win this game?

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:27.600
- I'm not gonna lie and pretend

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.350
that I have won all by myself.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.000
You're playing with your friends,

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.710
you only have three seconds to Google.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.540
But can you Google something that

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.620
points you in the right direction.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:36.890
- Definitely go with your gut.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.310
- The night I won, I
played a little more loose,

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.950
wasn't overthinking
it, and I think you are

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.140
in the right mindset to win the game.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.420
- Honestly from the richest HQ player,

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.792
coming from you, I
think I'm gonna win now.

00:05:48.792 --> 00:05:51.000
(game show music)

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:51.833
- [Eric Voiceover] I was so nervous

00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:53.944
while playing the game that
I actually forgot to talk.

00:05:53.944 --> 00:05:57.155
I just wanted to focus on the
questions and the answers.

00:05:57.155 --> 00:06:00.270
And that's what I did, and
I answered a lot right,

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.365
so many actually, that I
made it to the 12th question.

00:06:04.365 --> 00:06:06.730
It was the most stressful
moment in my life.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.060
This meant so much to me, I mean

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.420
not really but it did, sort of.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.690
- [Host] He does not
mention Grand Master Flash

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.240
and that is your answer baby.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.340
- Oh my God!

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.510
Oh my God, there is no one in the office

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.860
for me to share this with.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.860
$34.00, I won. (upbeat playful music)

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.852
I'm an HQ master, Mom.

00:06:34.852 --> 00:06:35.685
- [Eric's Mom] What?

00:06:35.685 --> 00:06:36.518
- I won HQ.

00:06:36.518 --> 00:06:37.640
- [Eric's Mom] No way, you're lying.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.092
- It's that unbelievable,
for me to win HQ?

00:06:40.092 --> 00:06:42.500
- [Eric's Mom] Yes.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.170
- Anyway, lesson learned,
Google helps a lot.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.431
Having a group of people,
like you know 20 people

00:06:47.431 --> 00:06:49.940
texting what they think
the answer is really helps.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:53.010
But sometimes you have to trust
yourself and not trust them.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.652
The game's fun, Eric approved, I love it.

00:06:55.652 --> 00:06:58.569
(fun upbeat music)

